By the spell of apt and the charm of cache,
Let Ubuntu's packages settle in place.
With idempotent whispers and no needless fright,
May every desired state be made right.
%
Gather, little facts, from kernel to shell;
Tell us which secrets the host would tell.
With gathered knowledge, both tidy and bright,
Ansible shall conjure the configuration right.
%
O handlers of change, awaken and run,
Only when summoned by tasks well begun.
Restart the service with graceful delight,
Then let it slumber throughout the night.
%
By become and sudo, ascend without fuss;
Grant just enough power, and no more than thus.
May privilege flow like a carefully measured stream,
While root's mighty crown remains part of the dream.
%
In /etc place order, in /var keep the lore;
Let templates render what was written before.
When variables dance and Jinja bells ring,
A stable configuration is the gift they shall bring.
%
Guard every secret with vault's silver key;
Keep passwords concealed from logs and the sea.
May encrypted variables, quiet and wise,
Remain hidden from curious terminal eyes.
%
With ufw as sentinel at the gate,
Permit what is needed and banish the late.
Let SSH pass safely, let stray ports depart;
May the firewall guard both machine and heart.
%
Cron sprites assemble at minutes precise,
Running backups as steady as ice.
When scheduled tasks whisper their tune,
May disks have room beneath sun and moon.
%
If a task should fail, let the playbook speak clear;
Name the true cause and banish vague fear.
With check mode's lantern held steady and bright,
Preview each change before casting it right.
%
From inventory hosts, both local and far,
Summon each server by its symbolic star.
With groups as circles and vars as the guide,
May Ubuntu's many spirits align side by side.
